WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.735
-Oh, my goodness. Come on.
Partner!

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.036
-Hi.

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:06.339
-My part-- My partner.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.741
-Blueberry.
-Blueberry muffin all the way.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:11.077
I can't believe we got that.
That's bizarre.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.244
-I feet really good about it.

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:13.278
-I feel really, really good
about it.

00:00:13.278 --> 00:00:14.447
Thank you for being here.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:15.882
Thank you for being in studio,
by the way.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:19.619
It means a lot to our audience
and to me and the band.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.619
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:21.988
You live in New York City.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.923
You've lived here for
10 years now.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:24.924
-I -- Mm-hmm.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.359
I moved here
when I was 16, yeah.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.694
-So you're a New Yorker.

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:32.532
-I don't want to, like,
adopt that without, like,

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.667
having permission
to say that, you know?

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.868
-I mean, you live in --

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:38.004
-I certainly love
the city so much,

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.939
but I feel like
there's a lot about me

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.608
that says that
I'm not from here.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.477
-You live in a studio apartment,
which is very New York.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.745
-Mm-hmm.
-Yeah.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.812
[ Applause ]

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:48.547
Yeah, I think it's one person.
-Thanks.

00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:50.349
That's what you normally hear
in a studio apartment --

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:52.785
one person like, "Yeah!"

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:56.922
You -- But you recently
got furniture.

00:00:56.922 --> 00:00:58.291
-It's taken 10 years,

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:01.160
but I finally buckled down
and I bought some furniture.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.695
For a very long time,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:07.032
I've had a mattress on the floor
and a light from IKEA.

00:01:07.032 --> 00:01:08.167
-Uh-huh.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:12.071
-And then I just felt like
maybe that --

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.873
It wasn't a good look
for me anymore,

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.674
and I thought I should grow up.

00:01:15.674 --> 00:01:17.409
-It's not --
Yeah, I mean, after a while,

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:19.946
yeah, if you can afford it,
furniture is fantastic.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.647
Yeah, it's great.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:24.216
-Oh! I will say, if you have
a mattress on the floor

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:25.851
for a very long time
and then you upgrade

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:28.721
to having a bed frame,
the process of getting

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.557
in and out of bed becomes
significantly easier.

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.526
It's less of, like,
a, like "Huh!"

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:36.429
and more of just like a,
"I'm getting out of bed now."

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.831
-Yeah, that's correct. Yes.
You don't have to like, "Hwah!"

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.566
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah, now it's a whole thing.

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.368
-It's just like
I casually get out of bed

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.536
and I just go about
my whole day.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.539
-It's better for you with the
higher up, yeah.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.508
This is your setup
in your house.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.610
You took a picture of you
having breakfast.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.078
This is what it looks like
in your apartment.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:54.246
-I love breakfast.
-Yeah, me too.

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:57.416
That's unbelievable.
That's your whole setup.

00:01:57.416 --> 00:02:00.719
-Mm-hmm.
-Yeah. So, you have your eggs.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:01.855
-Yeah, if you scroll in,
though, like,

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:02.922
some really well-made eggs.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.190
-That's not how
a photo works, Margaret.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:09.729
You can't -- you can't zoom in.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.164
You can't zoom in to any photo
and make it zoom in.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:15.167
But, alright, you have
eggs and toast, I see,

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.369
and maybe an avocado, perhaps?

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:19.138
-Yes.
-Oh, that's what I would have.

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:21.074
-Come over for
breakfast sometime.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:23.075
I have a table now!
-I'll bring a pillow.

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:25.411
-Yeah.
-Perfect.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.579
I do love that, though.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:29.081
It's kind of cool
that's what you did.

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:30.116
-Thank you.
-And now --

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.751
-You're the only one
that thinks that.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.252
-Yeah.

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:34.921
But now you have...

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.055
-Furniture.
-...furniture.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.957
So you have a bed.
Do you have a table?

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.826
-Bed, table, lamps...
-Yeah, you name it. Lamps.

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:41.861
-...chairs, sofa.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:43.296
-It's like we're playing
"Password" again.

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.365
Furniture!
-Furniture!

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.365
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:47.533
[ Dinging ]
Thank you.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.502
We got the password.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.337
I want to
talk to you about "Maid."

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.407
It's M-A-I-D, by the way,
if you're listening and don't --

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.641
because it could be,
"Oh, it's called 'Made,'"

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:56.642
and they don't find it.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:57.911
-Mm-hmm.
-M-A-I-D.

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.413
This is based on a true story,
a memoir.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.680
-It certainly is.
-Yeah.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.282
-I've said "certainly"
three times now.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.518
-Yeah, certainly -- Why?

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.619
-I'm nervous, Jimmy.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.421
I'm really nervous.
-Don't be nervous.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:09.422
You're winning so hard.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.823
You have no idea
how much you're winning.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.224
-Okay, here we are.

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:14.460
"Maid," with an "I."
-"Maid."

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.896
Your mom is Andie MacDowell,
who I love.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.230
-Me too.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.699
Well, of course you love mom.
She's acting with you.

00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:22.068
-I already said,
"I love you, Dad,"

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.569
and now, I feel like I should
say, "I love you, Mom."

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.204
Yes, she's acting with me.
-Yeah.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.839
I love you, mom, too, yeah.
And dad.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.208
I love your dad, too.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:30.242
-He's great.

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:31.777
-Yeah, I don't know him,
but I'm assuming.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.011
-You'd love him.
-I would, right?

00:03:33.011 --> 00:03:34.514
-Mm-hmm. You would.
Certainly.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:35.949
-Certainly.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:39.852
And now -- He probably has,
like, you know, lamp, tables.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:45.424
-Actually, no.
I -- He doesn't.

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:46.692
-Your dad
doesn't have furniture?

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:49.061
-He doesn't have
any of those things.

00:03:49.061 --> 00:03:50.697
No, I'm serious.
-Wait. What?

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.131
So your dad doesn't have --

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:54.634
-We're taking a real detour,
but, no, he has no furniture.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.635
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:59.372
-Wait. What is going --
What are you talking about?

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.173
-He lives in Panama,
on a construction site.

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:02.275
He has no furniture.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.109
But, okay,
back to the point -- "Maid."

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:05.445
M-A-I-D.

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.312
-Wow! Okay. Sorry.
This is so interesting.

00:04:07.312 --> 00:04:08.414
-My mom is in there.
-Yes, your mom's in there.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.648
Yeah, yeah.
-The show.

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:11.284
-The show. Alright,
let's talk about the show.

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:12.585
It's on Netflix.
-Uh-huh.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:15.621
-Okay, yeah, do you want to tell
everyone who you play?

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.957
-I do. I play Alex.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:21.627
-She is a young mother
who is trying to get out of a --

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.062
This is serious.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.798
She's trying to get out of an
emotionally abusive relationship

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.700
and she has a child.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.935
And she's trying to
escape poverty

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:33.106
and she starts cleaning homes
to take care of her kid.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.941
And it's about that.
-Yeah.

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:37.543
You're getting
great reviews for this.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:40.346
-And she has furniture.
-Yeah, there's furniture.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:41.881
No spoilers, Margaret.
No spoilers,

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.415
-Actually, no, she doesn't
have furniture either.

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:45.151
None of us have furniture.
-Yeah, it's interesting. Yeah.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.252
No, yeah, no spoilers.
None of us have furniture.

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.486
-Okay.

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:48.688
-I can't believe your dad
doesn't have furniture.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.289
That's interesting.
-None.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:51.758
-He's in Panama, you said?
-He is.

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:53.225
-Wow! That's so interesting.

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:55.761
On a construction site.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:56.996
-I'm really interested in
your dad.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:58.564
-I'll tell you
all about him later.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.199
-Yeah, we can hear about it
later, 'cause we're gonna be --

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.034
-He specifically said,
"Hey, Margaret,

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:04.269
don't talk about me tonight."

00:05:04.269 --> 00:05:06.239
-You did.
-I did.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:08.141
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:09.475
-And we spent most of
the interview

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:10.476
talking about your dad.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.577
-Yeah.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.778
-Wow. He just sounds
fascinating to me.

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:14.213
-I love him so much.
-Yeah, I love him, too.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:17.116
I mean, again,
I don't know him, but...

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.619
He's involved with you somehow,
I got to root for that person.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.321
-Okay. Thanks.
-For those people.

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:24.790
-Mm-hmm.
-And I think we should be pals.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.492
We should be friends.
-I want to be your friend.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.893
Ever since you
said that thing outside,

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:30.596
I've been trying to
orchestrate a friendship here.

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.665
-Yeah. I can see us,
like, you know,

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.101
getting together and playing,
like, a game night or something.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.568
-I love games.
-Right?

00:05:36.568 --> 00:05:37.569
Yeah.
-So much.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:39.439
-Yeah. What do you...

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:40.906
But you don't
own any games, right?

00:05:40.906 --> 00:05:42.208
So people have to bring it
over to your house.

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.877
-Yeah. Or, you know, you come up
with the games yourself.

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.011
Like, "What are you thinking
right now?"

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:47.312
That's what
they were saying that

00:05:47.312 --> 00:05:48.347
we should be practicing, right?

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:49.348
-Yeah.
You want to play that game?

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:50.549
-Yeah.

00:05:50.549 --> 00:05:54.120
-Alright, what are you
thinking about right now?

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.454
Your dad.

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:57.055
-He did it.

00:05:57.055 --> 00:05:58.257
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
[ Ding ]

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.326
See? I'm really good at this.

00:06:02.194 --> 00:06:04.963
You're fantastic in this show,
and I want to show a clip.

00:06:04.963 --> 00:06:07.132
Here is Margaret Qualley
in "Maid."

00:06:07.132 --> 00:06:08.333
Take a look at this.

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:09.401
-Are you drunk?

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:10.470
-I'm working on it.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.470
-And you've been out
all day biking.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.671
-So?

00:06:12.671 --> 00:06:13.873
-So Maddy has just been
stuck with your mom,

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.341
sitting on the couch,
watching "Jeopardy!"?

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:16.442
-No, no, no.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.877
They -- they watch
"Wheel of Fortune."

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:20.012
-Oh, this is funny to you?
What if she got sick?

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.447
-Okay...
-What if she got hurt?

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:22.815
What if she needed to
go to the E.R.?

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:24.183
-My mom would take her.

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.551
-Your mom?
-Yes.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.053
Your mom that spent half of your
childhood addicted to Oxy?

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:28.821
-Will you chill?
-I'm not going to chill, Sean.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.122
You have a rage problem.

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:31.757
-I don't know how you even say
it with a straight face.

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.759
-You have a rage problem
and you have a drinking problem

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:35.695
and you shouldn't have
custody of our kid

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:38.297
if you're going to
let your mommy do it for you.

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:39.732
-Margaret Qualley, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

